Licence and change log for the built font files in this directory
=================================================================

Every other file in public/fonts/ is fetched unmodified and carries its own
upstream terms. These four are DERIVED WORKS that we build ourselves, so this
notice is required to travel with them:

    latin-modern-roman-400.woff2
    latin-modern-roman-700.woff2
    latin-modern-roman-400-italic.woff2
    latin-modern-roman-700-italic.woff2

and the two files built from the same sources for PDF embedding:

    ../fonts-pdf/latin-modern-roman-400.ttf
    ../fonts-pdf/latin-modern-roman-700.ttf

They are built from Latin Modern Roman 10, version 2.005, by
scripts/make-built-fonts.py and scripts/make-pdf-fonts.py.

The original work is stated by its own README to be:

    Copyright 2003--2021 by B. Jackowski and J.M. Nowacki
    (on behalf of TeX Users Groups).
    This work is released under the GUST Font License.

and that README further records that the Type 1 outlines the original work was
derived from were placed in the public domain by the American Mathematical
Society. The GUST Font License is reproduced in full in section 3 below; it
puts the work under the LaTeX Project Public License version 1.3c, whose
clause 6 governs the derived files listed above.


1. The original work, and how to obtain a complete unmodified copy
------------------------------------------------------------------

Required by LPPL 1.3c clause 6d. The unmodified OpenType sources are:

    https://mirrors.ctan.org/fonts/lm/fonts/opentype/public/lm/lmroman10-regular.otf
    https://mirrors.ctan.org/fonts/lm/fonts/opentype/public/lm/lmroman10-bold.otf
    https://mirrors.ctan.org/fonts/lm/fonts/opentype/public/lm/lmroman10-italic.otf
    https://mirrors.ctan.org/fonts/lm/fonts/opentype/public/lm/lmroman10-bolditalic.otf

The whole package, including its own README and licence:

    https://mirrors.ctan.org/fonts/lm/

The exact bytes we built from, verified by scripts/make-built-fonts.py on every
run (SHA-256):

    1aa18cfefa58132c52ce5de70db1fd1154201c19cd2b2cdaffba4906a33e6852  lmroman10-regular.otf
    102fe06c430a8b681b2bf6876b7cd967ae4d47b4b6b41d915eb7913b726d9fb1  lmroman10-bold.otf
    c1fce25075567bb8dbf2151658c3b442690041db17a2d49fc9e55905ea5b7169  lmroman10-italic.otf
    c37a28eed7a6e03f792b98b5e5f637b2fcda378bb4855f99284f1a88fe35f124  lmroman10-bolditalic.otf


2. Complete and accurate log of the changes
--------------------------------------------

Required by LPPL 1.3c clause 6b. Nothing was drawn, redrawn or renamed; the
changes are entirely a change of container, plus one subsetting step forced by
a PDF-library constraint.

  a. CFF (cubic Bezier) outlines converted to a quadratic TrueType `glyf`
     table with fontTools' cu2qu, at a maximum error of 1 unit per 1000 em
     (fontmake's default; 0.0105 pt at a 10.5 pt body). The `CFF ` table was
     removed and `maxp` promoted from version 0.5 to 1.0 as that format
     requires. No outline was otherwise altered.

  b. The four web files were then repackaged as woff2. No glyph was removed:
     each keeps the full 794-codepoint character map of its source.

  c. The two PDF files (../fonts-pdf/) were additionally subset to the Latin,
     Greek, Cyrillic and Vietnamese ranges, leaving 581 codepoints, because
     the PDF library we embed with mis-renders a font whose glyph-offset table
     exceeds 131,070 bytes. The dropped codepoints are typesetting-engine
     specific ones the application never sets. No italic is built for PDF.

  d. No change was made to any name record. The families still identify
     themselves as Latin Modern Roman. The GUST Font License requests (clause
     1, and it states it is not legally required) that a derived work be
     renamed; we have not renamed, so that the face remains recognisable to
     the person choosing it, and this notice records the fact.

We are not affiliated with, and are not endorsed by, the authors of the
original work. Nothing in this product should be read as their having
supported or approved this build (LPPL 1.3c clause 6c).


