The marks font
=============================================================================

    cva-marks.ttf
    ../fonts-pdf/cva-marks-400.ttf

These two files are the SAME 1.6 KB font, built by scripts/make-marks-font.py.

It carries four glyphs and nothing else — U+25E6 white bullet, U+25AA small
square, U+2713 check mark, U+25C6 black diamond — plus a space and .notdef.
Measured over the whole bundle on 2026-09-16: none of the 158 PDF instances in
../fonts-pdf/ carries any of the four, and of the 257 web-font subset files
here only four carry the white bullet. So the four bullet styles that need
them had nowhere to come from: the canvas drew two of them as UA list-marker
shapes (no glyph, no text at all) and the other two from whatever font the
reader's own machine happened to have, and the PDF carried none of them.

Every outline in it is constructed by that script out of plain arithmetic —
two circles, a square, a diamond, and a polyline stroked to a width. No font
data, outline or metric is read, copied or derived from any other font. It is
therefore an original work of this repository and is covered by this
repository's own licence (see ../../LICENSE), like any other file we write.
